  "notes": [
    "A fresh policy is loaded for every rung. torch.compile is not reversible, and a compiled callable left on the module would contaminate the rungs below it.",
    "Rungs 0-3 keep regions on; 4-5 cannot, because a region boundary inside a compiled sample_actions forces a graph break. Compare rung 4/5's e2e with rung 3's e2e, never with its per-region numbers.",
    "`step_compile`/`whole_compile` use max-autotune-no-cudagraphs to get compilation WITHOUT CUDA graphs; the next rung adds reduce-overhead, whose difference from it is the CUDA-graph contribution. T003 found the stock modes differ by 1-4 % otherwise, so the mode change is a graph switch, not a codegen change.",
    "TF32 is set explicitly on every rung rather than inherited from config.compile_model, so that the precision factor is separated from the compilation factor instead of moving with it."
  ],
